// Formative practice quiz for custom-hooks. Low-stakes; answers are visible by design. First draft, not yet reviewed.
$CATEGORY: react/effects-routing-and-rendering/custom-hooks

::custom-hooks o1 - naming::You extract fetching logic that calls useState and useEffect into a new function. What should it be called?{
=A name starting with use, such as useFetch#Correct. The prefix marks it as a Hook, so the Rules of Hooks apply and linters can check it.
~A capitalized name, such as FetchData#Not quite. A capital letter marks a component, which returns JSX.
~Any name, because the runtime does not care#Not quite. Linting and readers rely on the use prefix to apply the Rules of Hooks.
~A name ending in Hook#Not quite. The convention is the prefix use.
}

::custom-hooks o1 - when to extract::Three components each repeat the same useState and useEffect code to load data. What is the best refactor?{
=Extract a custom Hook that holds that logic#Correct. A custom Hook reuses stateful logic across components.
~Keep the copies so each can change later#Not quite. Copies drift and every fix must be repeated.
~Move the logic into a plain variable#Not quite. A variable cannot hold logic that needs state and Effects.
~Put it in index.html#Not quite. That file is a page shell, and it runs no React logic.
}

::custom-hooks o2 - independent state::Two components call the same useCounter Hook. One calls its add function. What happens to the other?{
=Nothing, because each caller has its own state#Correct. Each call to a Hook creates separate state.
~It updates too, because the Hook is shared#Not quite. The logic is shared, not the state.
~It resets to zero#Not quite. The other component is untouched.
~React throws an error#Not quite. Calling a Hook from many components is normal.
}

::custom-hooks o3 - plain function enough::A helper takes a date and returns formatted text, calling no Hooks. What should it be?{
=A plain function with an ordinary name#Correct. With no Hooks inside, it need not follow Hook rules, and it can be called anywhere.
~A custom Hook named useFormatDate#Not quite. The use prefix would add Hook rules for no benefit.
~A component#Not quite. It returns text, not a piece of UI to render as a tag.
~An Effect#Not quite. Nothing here needs to synchronize with the outside world.
}
